In the Spring 2026 edition of the Metaculus Cup one question concerned the
number of runs in the knockout stage of the World Baseball Classic (WBC)
in 2026.
</p>



<p>
The community predicted a mean of just under 70 runs, with a spread of 60–80. My
prediction was 60 runs, with a spread of 42–80. The actual number ended up being
59 runs – nearly exactly what I predicted. Let&rsquo;s see how that was done.
</p>



<p>
First, there&rsquo;s a sloppy way of making a quick guess. It&rsquo;s not very interesting,
but it&rsquo;s a good baseline. Once we have that, we&rsquo;ll dig into modeling counts on a
more granular level, and that&rsquo;s when it gets interesting. Those techniques can
be used for all sorts of counts, not just sports prediction!
</p>



